{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790990112,"nonce":"qCQwxgkQgEhM6IZxxgewGhJS7Yo=","title":"Interpreter lets an invalid array cast through instead of throwing","message":"An `Array\u003cFloat\u003e` cast to `Array\u003cNull\u003cFloat\u003e\u003e` (an ArrayBytes_Float where an ArrayObj is expected) must throw \"Can't cast hl.types.ArrayBytes_Float to hl.types.ArrayObj\" at the cast. Stock HashLink 1.15 does, and so does Ash's jit. Ash's interp and hybrid let the cast through; the program then fails later with a misleading \"Null access\", or would read the wrong layout.\n\nReproducer, tracked in ashui: tests/fixtures/ash/array_variance/run.sh (Variance.hx). It builds the program and runs it in all three modes:\n\n    interp: Uncaught exception: Null access\n    hybrid: Uncaught exception: Null access\n    jit: Uncaught exception: Can't cast hl.types.ArrayBytes_Float to hl.types.ArrayObj\n\nStock hl 1.15 (on the NUC): Uncaught exception: Can't cast hl.types.ArrayBytes_Float to hl.types.ArrayObj, Called from $Main.parse.\n\nThe Haxe that produces it: a switch whose branches are `[0.0, 0.0, 1.0, maybeNull]` (typed Array\u003cNull\u003cFloat\u003e\u003e) and `[0.0, 0.0, 10.0, 10.0]` (Array\u003cFloat\u003e); the switch is typed Array\u003cNull\u003cFloat\u003e\u003e and the second branch is cast. Found in ashui's SVG parser, which no longer does this.","files":null}]}